// Title: Network Connection Initiated From Users\Public Folder
// Sigma ID: bcb03938-9f8b-487d-8d86-e480691e1d71
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-05-31 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects a network connection initiated from a process located in the "C:\Users\Public" folder.
//   Attacker are known to drop their malicious payloads and malware in this directory as its
//   writable by everyone. Use this rule to hunt for potential suspicious or uncommon activity in
//   your environement.
// False positives:
//   - Likely from legitimate third party application that execute from the "Public" directory.
// References:
//   - https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/17pSTDNpa0sf6pHeRhusvWG6rThciE8CsXTSlDUAZDyo
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-threat-hunting/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_susp_initaited_public_folder.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains ":\\Users\\Public\\" and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains ":\\Users\\Public\\IBM\\ClientSolutions\\Start_Programs\\"))
